# Template for `.env` — a personal record of the PRODUCTION values only.
# Nothing reads this file: not the app, not wrangler, not vitest. Local dev
# reads `.dev.vars`; production reads Cloudflare Worker secrets, which are
# write-only (Cloudflare cannot show them back to you). Keep your own copy here
# so a rotated value is not lost.
#
# Set each of these in production with:
#   npx wrangler secret put <NAME>

# ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Login credentials
# The single account that may open the calculator.
# generate a password: openssl rand -base64 24
# ──────────────────────────────────────────
AUTH_USER=
AUTH_PASS=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Session signing key
# HMAC-SHA256 key for the `rim_session` cookie. Rotating it logs everyone out.
# generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# ──────────────────────────────────────────
SESSION_SECRET=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Local HTTPS escape hatch — LOCAL ONLY, never set in production.
# Listed here only so its absence is a deliberate choice rather than an
# oversight. Setting it to "1" in production disables the plaintext upgrade
# and the Secure flag on the session cookie. Local value lives in `.dev.vars`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────
# ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=
